"Celena North High caps B-rank admissions at 25% for most programs and 5% for the hero course."
"An entrance physical is required to begin a hero-track application."
"Admission also takes physical testing, several interviews, and power and combat assessments."
"The hero track has higher credit requirements per quarter."
"B-ranks who get in are perfectly specced and must truly want it."
"Hero schools are hard on B-ranks and oddballs; a Rabbit wanting hero training is rare."
"Admissions run six times a year; about 250 apply per cycle and forty to fifty are admitted."
"About a dozen B-ranks get in a year, sometimes none; applicants must be under seventeen."
"B-ranks face three interviews, the first a B-only round; returning applicants get five minutes."
"Test day includes a talent assessment, drug testing, a trait-assisted run and a combat assessment."
"Combat assessments pit applicants in duels and in rescue games of heroes against villains."
"Applicants may refuse bad matchups, but those who leave early are not admitted."
"Strugglers are given at least one terrible matchup."
"Alumni heroes evaluate and vote on candidates."
"A final question, under NDA, warns of full-realism training and mental manipulation to come."
"Performance-enhancing wordchains are allowed on test day."
"Hero-track graduates go on automatically to Celena North University."
